<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Zator</h1><p class="st-meta">1445 CE – 1494 CE · capital Zator</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Silesian Piast duchy on the upper Vistula, sold to the Polish king in 1494.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zator, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Oswiecim</a>, was created in 1445 when the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-oswiecim">Duchy of Oswiecim</a> was divided among the sons of Duke Casimir I, and Wenceslaus I took the Zator lands. Like Oswiecim, it was formally a fief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy was a small agricultural land in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> valley, known for its fish ponds, where the breeding of carp later became a local speciality. Its dukes were minor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piasts</a> with limited resources, and the duchy was further divided among Wenceslaus's sons.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1494 Duke Jan V sold Zator to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-albert">King John I Albert</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. It was incorporated, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Oswiecim</a>, into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1385-1569">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1385-1569) in 1564.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-zator.jpg" alt="Duchy of Zator" width="320" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Jerzy Strzelecki · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zator_(js).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1445 CE – 1494 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zator</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wenceslaus I of Zator, Jan V of Zator</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Poland</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zator</dd></dl></aside></div>
